.SH Signal Configuration
The signals are configured via \f[CR]sigaction()\f[R] in
\f[CR]setup_signals()\f[R]:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]SIGINT\f[R] and \f[CR]SIGTERM\f[R] are installed \f[B]without\f[R]
\f[CR]SA_RESTART\f[R], so that \f[CR]accept()\f[R] in the main loop
returns \f[CR]EINTR\f[R] and the loop can check
\f[CR]server_running\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]SIGCHLD\f[R] is installed \f[B]with\f[R] \f[CR]SA_RESTART\f[R], so
that child reaping does not interrupt ongoing I/O operations.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]SIGPIPE\f[R] is installed with \f[CR]SIG_IGN\f[R] (not this
handler), so writes to closed sockets return \f[CR]EPIPE\f[R] instead of
killing the process.
